    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d318">

                <pb facs="0394" n="292" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg292"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/6227: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Tientsin (Lockhart) to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tientsin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-04-26T15:00:00+08:00">April 26, 1933—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 26—5:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Withdrawal Manchukuo forces has now reached point between Changli and
                    Chinwangtao. No fighting and except for Chinese armored train no Chinese
                    military units of regular establishment have crossed to east bank Lwan River
                    according to best information <pb facs="0395" n="293" xml:id="pg293"/> available
                    Tientsin. As situation develops along the railway between Lwanchow and
                    Chinwangtao the inference becomes clearer that the withdrawal is the result of
                    an agreement or understanding as intimated in my April 24, 3 p.m.<anchor n="7"
                        xml:id="d318-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
